canonicalCurve -- Compute a random canonical curve of genus less or equal to 14
*******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        I=(random canonicalCurve)(g,S)
  * Inputs:
      * g, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the genus
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, homogeneous
        coordinate ring of $\PP^{ g-1}$
  * Outputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, of a canonical curve $C$ of
        genus $g$

Description
===========

Compute a random canonical curve of genus $g \le{} 14$, based on the proofs of
unirationality of $M_g$ by Severi, Sernesi, Chang-Ran and Verra.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : setRandomSeed "alpha";                        |
| -- setting random seed to 10206284518             |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : g=14;                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : FF=ZZ/10007;                                  |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : R=FF[x_0..x_(g-1)];                           |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : time betti(I=(random canonicalCurve)(g,R))    |
| -- used 8.65568s (cpu); 6.76278s (thread); 0s (gc)|
|                                                   |
|            0  1                                   |
|o5 = total: 1 66                                   |
|         0: 1  .                                   |
|         1: . 66                                   |
|                                                   |
|o5 : BettiTally                                    |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : genus I == g and degree I ==2*g-2             |
|                                                   |
|o6 = true                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+

